Subject: segmented-control-v2: a 1px track with an inset thumb

What: the track draws a 1px border with 2px padding and a 2px gap, and the pressed item sits inside it as a thumb with its own 1px ring.
Why: the 0.5px box-shadow rings vanished on edges that landed on a fractional device pixel, so the control read as broken, and the edge-to-edge pressed item drew its ring on top of the track's.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/segmented-control-v2.css b/src/v2/components/segmented-control-v2.css
index 513899f3c8..4b79153fc7 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/segmented-control-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/segmented-control-v2.css
@@ -14,15 +14,15 @@
   box-sizing: border-box;
   display: flex;
   flex-direction: row;
-  align-items: center;
-  padding: 0;
+  align-items: stretch;
+  gap: 2px;
+  padding: 2px;
   width: 232px;
   max-width: 100%;
   height: 28px;
   background: var(--v2-background-bg-layer-01);
-  border: none;
+  border: 1px solid var(--v2-border-border-base);
   border-radius: var(--radius-md);
-  box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5px var(--v2-border-border-base);
   flex: none;
 }
 
@@ -35,10 +35,10 @@
   padding: 0 12px;
   flex: 1 1 0;
   min-width: 0;
-  height: 28px;
+  height: auto;
   margin: 0;
   border: none;
-  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
   background: transparent;
   box-shadow: none;
   cursor: pointer;
@@ -70,8 +70,7 @@
 .ui-segmented-control-v2-item:where([data-pressed]) {
   background: var(--v2-background-bg-base);
   color: var(--v2-text-text-base);
-  box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5px var(--v2-border-border-strong);
-  z-index: 1;
+  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--v2-border-border-base);
 }
 
 [data-slot="segmented-control-v2-item-label"] {
